      <Comment source="AU4FS-4, SRI, caspi">Volatile sulfanylalkanols are a component of the odorous compounds produced by bacteria acting on axillary (underarm) secretions. A major compound is |FRAME: CPD-21078| |CITS: [17191896][17191898][17191839]|, which is secreted from the apocrine glands in the axilla as |FRAME: CPD-21107| |CITS: [17192014]|, and is converted to its final form by the sequential action of two bacterial enzymes |CITS: [18515361]|.</Comment>
